          "content": "The duplicate is fixed — `01_deref.c` is now `02_deref.c`, so the sequence runs cleanly `01, 02, 03, ...` with no gaps or collisions:\n\n```\n01-pointers/\n  01_address.c\n  02_deref.c\n  03_passing_pointers_as_function_args.c\n  04_two_labels_one_box.c\n  05_swap.c\n  06_box_and_labels.c\n  07_functions_and_pointers.c\n  08_arrays_are_pointers.c\n  09_array_decays.c\n```\n\nThe structure is in good shape now: numbered topic folder, separate `app/` for the capstone, a `.gitignore`, and no build artifacts tracked.\n\nOne tiny leftover: `20261006.log` is still sitting in the root. If your `.gitignore` covers `*.log` it won't be committed, but it's safe to delete since it's just a stray log. Want me to remove it?\n\nOtherwise you're set. Whenever you're ready to continue learning, lesson 6 would be **NULL pointers** (and the classic crash from dereferencing NULL) followed by **`malloc`/`free`** for dynamic memory — the point where pointers become essential rather than just convenient.",
