          "message_id": "5f215164-2cb9-42ac-8cdf-5c65e220ec1d",
          "content": "Got it — `02` is reserved for arrays, so structs go in `03-structs/`. That makes sense as an ordering too, since arrays are the more fundamental topic and naturally come before structs.\n\nQuick question before I build the first struct lesson: do you want me to **create the empty `02-arrays/` folder now** as a placeholder (so the numbering is visible and reserved), or leave it until you're ready to work on arrays and just start `03-structs/` directly?\n\nEither way, when you're ready for structs, I'll follow the same style you've been using — numbered files (`01_...`, `02_...`), heavy teaching comments, each a standalone program with a `main`. The natural progression for structs would be:\n\n1. `01_struct_basics.c` — defining a struct, the `.` operator\n2. `02_struct_pointers.c` — pointers to structs and the `->` operator (and why `->` exists)\n3. `03_passing_structs.c` — by value vs. by pointer (ties back to your benchmark)\n4. `04_linked_list.c` — the payoff: a struct that points to itself\n\nWant me to go ahead and start `03-structs/01_struct_basics.c`, and should I create the `02-arrays/` placeholder?",
