          "content": "No problem — exercises can wait until you're in the mood. Learning by exploring and discussing is just as valid.\n\nIf you want to keep building intuition without the work of exercises, here are some low-effort ways to continue:\n\n- **I explain, you absorb.** I can keep walking through the mental models — like unpacking that `&arr` vs `arr` subtlety, or showing why strings are just `char` arrays with a `\\0` at the end.\n- **Watch instead of write.** I can write a small program that *visualizes* something (prints addresses, shows memory layout) and run it, so you just read the output and see the concept in action — no work on your end.\n- **Just chat about it.** Ask me whatever's still fuzzy and we talk it through.\n- **Take a break entirely.** Come back to the linked list or arrays whenever you feel like it.\n\nWhat sounds good right now?",
