          "content": "I need your pwsh profile path to add the alias. Since `pwsh` isn't reachable from the tool's shell, the standard pwsh 7 profile location is:\n\n```\nC:\\Users\\ngandhi\\Documents\\PowerShell\\Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1\n```\n\n(or under your OneDrive-redirected Documents, which is what showed up earlier). Rather than guess, could you run this in your `pwsh` terminal and paste the output?\n\n```powershell\n$PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts\n```\n\nThat gives me the exact file to edit. \n\nMeanwhile, here's the line that needs to go in it:\n\n```powershell\nSet-Alias -Name make -Value mingw32-make\n```\n\nIf you'd rather just do it yourself in one shot, run these two commands in your `pwsh` terminal:\n\n```powershell\nif (!(Test-Path $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts)) { New-Item -ItemType File -Path $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts -Force }\nAdd-Content -Path $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts -Value \"`nSet-Alias -Name make -Value mingw32-make\"\n```\n\nThen reload with `. $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts` (or open a new terminal), and `make clean` will work as an alias for `mingw32-make clean`.\n\nWant me to write the alias file for you instead? If so, just paste the output of `$PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts` and I'll create/edit it directly.",
