          "message_id": "51a22770-6972-4b1b-9b8e-82e92fd6a7f2",
          "content": "The profile is created with the alias. To use it in your current session, reload the profile (or just open a new terminal):\n\n```powershell\n. $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts\n```\n\nThen verify it works:\n\n```powershell\nmake clean\n```\n\nThat should now run `mingw32-make clean` and remove any `.exe` files.\n\nOne heads-up: PowerShell aliases can't carry arguments, but that's fine here — `make clean` works because `clean` is passed as an argument to the aliased command, not baked into the alias. So `make build`, `make list`, and `make clean` all work as expected.\n\nThat wraps up the Makefile and alias setup. Whenever you're ready to get back to C, the linked list in `03-structs/` or `realloc` are waiting.",
