    "No Makefile yet. I can see `.exe` files scattered in the topic folders (e.g. two in `01-pointers/`). \n\nOne important consideration: your environment is Windows, but the shell is PowerShell/`sh`-ish (I saw `.profile loaded [vi mode]`), and you're using MinGW gcc. The `del` command is Windows-native but may not work the same under your shell. The most portable approach for a Makefile that MinGW's `mingw32-make` runs is to use a cross-platform recursive delete. Let me write a Makefile with a `clean` target plus a couple of convenience targets.\n[Tool uses: fs_write]",
